# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files since the code is
#   intended to run in multiple environments; otherwise, check them in:
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version control.
#   However, in case of collaboration, if the platform is not standard, the lock file can be ignored.
#Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   poetry.lock is usually committed unless you want to rely on pyproject.toml's specifications
#poetry.lock

# pdm
